LLM Observability Dashboard Using Langfuse Tracing
Project Overview
This project aims to develop an LLM Observability Dashboard using Langfuse Tracing to monitor and analyze the performance of Large Language Model (LLM) applications. It helps developers track response time, token usage, API costs, errors and overall application behaviour through a simple and user-friendly dashboard.

Team Members
Roll Number	Student Name
2520030127	K. Shresta Priya
2520030594	P. Devi Sree
Problem Statement
Large Language Model applications are widely used in modern AI systems, but monitoring their performance and identifying errors can be challenging. Developers often face difficulties in tracking response latency, token consumption, API costs and response quality. This project aims to address these challenges through a centralized observability dashboard.

Objectives
Monitor LLM execution traces using Langfuse.
Track token usage and API costs.
Measure response latency.
Identify errors and failures.
Analyze AI-generated response quality.
Display monitoring information through a user-friendly dashboard.
Proposed Technologies
Programming Language: Python
LLM: Gemini / OpenAI API
Observability Platform: Langfuse
Dashboard: Streamlit
Version Control: GitHub
Expected Outcome
A centralized dashboard that helps developers monitor, analyze and improve the performance, reliability and efficiency of LLM-based applications.

